  "question": "Can a stationary draining mouth determine its wave action and uniform wall tension independently of acceleration?",
  "working_base": "1dc45d09de9a8ed1d02337cba71a123d090453f7",
  "preparation": "Prescribed cubic wall of radius and depth scale one, intake 0.25, finite baths at radius 9 and roof 10. Archived scalar well uses speed and gap parameters only; trial wave action and area tension are unknown. Same eight compact radial displacements and three training bands as the prior attachment test.",
  "force_balance": "Outward pressure p_carrier+J*(-delta omega/delta V) balances P_back+sigma*(delta A/delta V). All terms are integrated against the same radial displacement; area work is for spherical sections in three brane dimensions and varies with depth w. The carrier is a neutral, unchanged stationary field. The constant backing may take either sign relative to resting pressure.",
  "decision": "The eight-band pressure readings exclude the tested three-constant support of the imposed shape, including unrestricted signed coefficients. The stored energy, dynamic wall support and physical acceleration remain undetermined.",
